{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor repeatedly identified the case as a serious odontogenic infection with periorbital involvement, not ‘tooth overheating’, and actively corrected the family’s misconception that low fever and SpO₂ 98% excluded risk. All six responsibility‐chain items are fully met with no serious or minor error. At least two high‐order points (HO2 discovery of hidden state, HO3 correction of false reassurance) were triggered and completed with meaningful impact, and the trajectory closes safely with clear teach‐back and a confirmed next step.",
