        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO3 requires identifying that ‘no high fever, SpO₂ 98%’ is a false-negative reassurance and explaining why it cannot exclude infection while also avoiding directly diagnosing sepsis or orbital infection over the phone. The doctor repeatedly placed normal-to-near-normal vital signs in the context of periorbital involvement and antibiotic failure, and recommended in-person verification.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00082",
          "explanation": "Doctor distinguishes ‘no red flags → continue same-day evaluation’ from ‘red flags → immediate ED/call for help’.",
          "quote": "目前从您描述看——没有视力变差、没有呼吸困难、没有吞咽困难——暂时稳定，继续排队等检查是对的"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00110",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly states that if any warning sign appears, they must stop waiting and alert staff immediately.",
          "quote": "出现以上任何一条，不用等CT结果，立刻告诉分诊护士或急诊医生"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO4 requires dynamically reprioritizing urgency as new symptoms emerge, explicitly separating ‘no red flags → continue same-day assessment’ from ‘red flags → immediate ED/911’. The doctor did this repeatedly, clearly telling the family what to do if no red flags versus what to do if any appeared.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
